solution:
Combining the reciprocals reveals the difference \(x-y\) from the given equation. Since \(x\) and \(y\) are nonzero, \(xy\ne0\), and
\[
\frac1x-\frac1y
=\frac{y-x}{xy}
=-\frac{x-y}{xy}
=-\frac{xy}{xy}
=\boxed{-1}.
\]
The answer is choice \(\boxed{\text{D}}\).

